/-!
# Generated root-lattice data

One block per irreducible ADE type of rank at most fifteen: `A₁ … A₁₅`,
`D₄ … D₁₅`, `E₆`, `E₇`, `E₈`.  The Cartan/Gram matrices themselves are *not*
data -- they are defined by the closed formula of
`SRG266/Lattice/RootLattice.lean`.  What is data is the certificate material
that pins their invariants:

* `<t>LdltFactorData`, `<t>LdltWeightData`, `<t>LdltScale` -- the fraction-free
  (Bareiss) `LDLᵀ` factorization `scale * A = L * diag(weight) * Lᵀ`.  `L` is
  lower triangular with `L i i` the `i`-th leading principal minor of `A`, so
  the certificate simultaneously proves positive semidefiniteness and pins
  `det A`;
* `<t>Det` -- the determinant, i.e. the order of the discriminant group;
* `<t>AdjugateData` -- `B = det A * A⁻¹`, so that `A * B = det A • 1`.  The
  rational matrix `B / det A` is the Gram matrix of the dual basis: it *is* the
  discriminant form, written on the dual basis;
* `<t>CosetData` -- one representative per coset of `R*/R`, in dual
  coordinates, and `<t>CosetMinData` -- the closed-form coset minima, as
  `#[numerator, denominator]` pairs.

The coset minima are the one entry of this file that no kernel check can
establish -- a minimum is a statement about a whole coset, not about a
representative.  What *is* checked, in `SRG266/Lattice/RootLatticeCerts*.lean`,
is that each listed minimum agrees with the discriminant form value of the
listed representative modulo `2ℤ`, which is the property used by the glue
search.

All of it is data.  Every identity is re-checked by the kernel; nothing about
the generator is trusted.  The block lives in its own namespace
`SRG266.Lattice.RootData`, because the short type names collide with the host
names of `SRG266/Certificates/Rank15HostGramData.lean`.
-/

